@startuml matrix-message-injection
!theme plain
' Updated: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13)
title Matrix message -> provider mailbox -> bridge admission -> durable host enqueue -> dispatch -> applied; output through an audience projection

database "Matrix (a2a)" as MX
participant "Matrix provider\n(child process)" as MP
participant "Bridge\n(M3)" as BR
database "Bridge store\n(id claims, mailbox,\noutbox, audit)" as BS
participant "Trust\n(curator-trust, mandates)" as T
participant "Session host\n(admission, inbox)" as SH
participant "Context Engine\n(dispatcher)" as CE
participant "Harness" as H

MX -> MP: new event in #X-repo (sync)
MP -> MP: persist to mailbox (fsync), then advance carrier cursor
MP -> BR: envelope{binding_handle, swarm-envelope/2 bytes}
BR -> BR: principal from handle + verified carrier identity\n(claimed_sender is data only)
BR -> T: exact-byte signature, enrolled key,\ngrant for action on target, revocation
T --> BR: result

BR -> BS: atomic: claim (principal, id) -> envelope_digest of complete canonical signed intent,\nverdict, admission record
alt same principal/id, same canonical signed-intent digest
  BR -> MP: original intent-bound receipt (exact retry; no new enqueue)
else same principal/id, changed signed intent (even with same body) / reflection / expired / wrong target
  BR -> BS: audit
  BR -> MP: receipt refused{reason}
else new admitted intent
  alt unsigned
    BR -> BS: quarantine: body stays in the mailbox
    BR -> SH: enqueue(doorbell: channel, claimed sender, ids)
  else signed peer
    BR -> SH: enqueue(data, UNTRUSTED PEER EVENTS frame)
  else operator-signed user_turn
    BR -> SH: enqueue(user_turn, authoritative)
  end

  SH -> SH: admit(): bridge identity, grant, expiry, binding rev;\nidem_key identifies principal/id; compare stored envelope_digest\nbefore enqueue or receipt lookup; changed intent = id_conflict
  alt storage failure or refused
    SH --> BR: refused{storage or reason}
    BR -> MP: receipt refused
  else persisted (fsync)
    SH --> BR: ack{host_seq}
    BR -> MP: receipt queued
  end
end

== Dispatch (fence open, turn boundary) ==
CE -> SH: admit() again: revocation, expiry, fence, readiness
alt session idle and ready
  CE -> H: write input with input_marker (adapter)
  CE -> SH: dispatched{host_seq, execution_id}
  H --> CE: adapter echo of input_marker
  CE -> SH: applied
else working
  CE -> CE: wait for the turn boundary (or native steer)
else interaction pending, human lease held, or unknown state
  CE -> CE: hold (queued); unknown parks
else holder died after dispatch
  CE -> SH: unknown: reconcile before any replay
end
SH -> BR: staged receipt (dispatched / applied / refused / expired / unknown)
BR -> MP: receipt{id, state}
MP -> MX: ack (mailbox receipt)

== Output ==
H -> CE: events (text, tool calls, turn.completed)
CE -> CE: reserve/charge retained debt before journal append (host store)
note right of CE
  Before durable acceptance: charge producer and aggregate retained debt;
  debt survives replacement/retirement; bound buffers and refusals.
  Producer output cannot consume control/evidence reserve.
  Host storage contract owns budgets/retention and qualification (ADM §5).
  Storage failure never produces a durable ack.
end note
CE -> BR: observe(OutputEvent)
BR -> BR: audience projection: final_text by default;\ntool calls only with a transcript grant
BR -> BS: outbox item (origin id kept for reflection checks)
BR -> MP: output{binding_handle, projected event}
MP -> MX: post reply in the same thread
@enduml
